RF.put("questb:b34",{"8594":{"id":8594,"t":"Mantle of the Oracle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Command Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Rebirth Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nMantle of the Oracle\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Priest Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8594\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Mantle of the Oracle this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8514":{"id":8514,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Medium Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 medium leather to Private Porter at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n10 Medium Leather Tattered Chest 0 % , Battered Chest 0 % , Solid Chest 0 % , Alliance Strongbox 0 % and 4 more","desc":"Yes sir/ma'am, looks like we've collected $2063w pieces of medium leather to date. I know it's a lot to ask, but if you're still willing, I could use your help in attempting to put a dent in the rest of my quota.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Yes sir, looks like we've collected many pieces of medium leather, but we need more. I can assure you that it will all be put to good use; not one piece will get wasted. I know it's a lot to ask, but if you're still willing, I could use your help in attempting to put a dent in the rest of my quota.","done":"Golly, that sure is a lot of medium leather that you've brought round, sir! I'm gonna make sure that all of that gets put to proper use, yes indeed. With your help we'll have filled our estimation for medium leather in no time!\nThanks, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":33.2,"n":"Private Porter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"92434":{"id":92434,"t":"Blood in the streets","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find a way into Dalaran along the Lordamere Lake.\nFind a way into Dalaran along the Lordamere Lake\nProvided: Grimy Key","desc":"Whatever caused Dalaran's barrier to lower has left the city in turmoil. With you having dealt with their patrols, there is no better time than now to make our way inside and discover their secrets.\nTake the key you found at the internment camp and seek out their sewers along the northern border of the city. With luck, those mages had no reason to put a ward over such a... disagreeable point of entry.\nHillsbrad Foothills Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.6,"y":20.8,"n":"Magus Wordeen Voidglare","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":68.6,"y":45.2,"n":"Image of Archmage Modera","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"514":{"id":514,"t":"Letter to Stormpike","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Cleverly Encrypted Letter to Prospector Stormpike in Ironforge.\nCleverly Encrypted Letter\nProvided: Cleverly Encrypted Letter","desc":"I have a colleague in Ironforge who may be able to help decrypt this letter. Go to the Library in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge and speak with Prospector Stormpike. Tell him I sent you and show him the letter. If there's anyone north of Blackrock Spire who can read this, it is he.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Dibbs from Southshore sent you, did he? How is the old bookworm doing?","done":"Ah, encryption! A specialty of mine. Let me see here...\nHillsbrad Foothills Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.6,"y":57.1,"n":"Loremaster Dibbs","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23,"n":"Prospector Stormpike","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8114":{"id":8114,"t":"Control Four Bases","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Enter Arathi Basin, capture and control four bases at the same time, and then return to Field Marshal Oslight at Refuge Pointe.","desc":"‹name›, you have taken the battle of Arathi Basin to our enemies and earned great honors in that field of battle. You have shown us your worth as a ‹class›, and you have shown our enemies that we will not submit to their villainy!\nBecause of your proven value to us, I have a difficult task for you. I want you to take and hold at least four of the bases in Arathi Basin. If you can do that, then we will not only secure critical resources, we will show the Horde our dominance!\nGo, ‹name›, and good fortune.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Field Marshal Oslight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"674":{"id":674,"t":"Raising Spirits","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give the Raptor Talon Amulet to Gor'mul.\nRaptor Talon Amulet\nProvided: Raptor Talon Amulet","desc":"Here, take this amulet to Gor'mul, and see if the raptors' strength can awaken the flame of the warrior that once burned through his veins.","rew":"Experience: 270\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"What hope is there when the hand of a coward can slay the mightiest of the mightiest? What hope, I ask you!","done":"What is this? Polished bone. What use have I for polished bone? Will a trinket restore the Horde to its glory?","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":72.6,"y":33.9,"n":"Gor'mul","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"8994":{"id":8994,"t":"Final Preparations","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 40 Blackrock Bracers and acquire a Flask of Supreme Power. Return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\n40 Blackrock Bracer Blackhand Dragon Handler 80 % , Summoned Blackhand Veteran 80 % , Summoned Blackhand Dreadweaver 80 % , Blackhand Iron Guard 80 % and 4 more\nFlask of Supreme Power\nProvided: Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"We're nearly there, ‹class›. All that is left is to retrieve a few more components so that I can attune the brazier and enable it to beckon forth Lord Valthalak.\nTo begin I must ask you to journey forth into Blackrock Spire and slay the orcs therein. They wear bracers that contain trace metals that I will need, so I'll need more than a few to extract the right amount out of them. Then, to complete the imbuing process, you'll need to bring me a Flask of Supreme Power.\nGood luck, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"We've come a long way, ‹name›, and I just wanted to say that no matter what happens, thank you! You've put yourself in mortal danger to try to help the surviving members of our mercenary company, The Veiled Blade, and as far as I'm concerned, you're one of us now.","done":"That's it then. I'll extract the metal from the bracers and imbue the brazier with these final components. Then it will be ready for you to summon Lord Valthalak, and finally return his spirit amulet to him.\nYou've come quite a distance, ‹name›, don't falter now that the end is in sight!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"2754":{"id":2754,"t":"Horns of Frenzy","lv":36,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring two Solid Iron Mauls, two Silvered Bronze Boots, and two Silvered Bronze Gauntlets to Orokk Omosh in Orgrimmar.\n2 Solid Iron Maul\n2 Silvered Bronze Boots\n2 Silvered Bronze Gauntlets","desc":"The final lesson Orokk teaches you, ‹name›. To the sacred anvil and forge you return! Bring for Orokk two solid iron mauls, two silvered bronze boots, and two silvered bronze gauntlets.\nSee the fear in their eyes as you approach!","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Barbaric Iron Helm\nExperience: 2,800","back":"Show the iron who is in charge, ‹name›!","done":"Astounding! You have learned the way of the Omosh, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":79.2,"y":22.4,"n":"Orokk Omosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97954":{"id":97954,"t":"Camping 101 engineering","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Graham Van Talen in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your engineering skill to 20","desc":"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":75.6,"y":73.2,"n":"Graham Van Talen","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94274":{"id":94274,"t":"Craftsmans writ golden scale coif","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Golden Scale Coif\nGolden Scale Coif","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Golden Scale Coif, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Golden Scale Coif Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94274","cats":["crafting"]},"94354":{"id":94354,"t":"Craftsmans writ runecloth boots","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Runecloth Boots\nRunecloth Boots","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Runecloth Boots, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Runecloth Boots Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94354","cats":["crafting"]},"994":{"id":994,"t":"Escape Through Force","lv":22,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Volcor until you reach the road, then speak to Terenthis in Auberdine.","desc":"All right, ‹name›, force it is. Let's get out of here as soon as you're ready. We'll fight our way down to the road--Grimclaw should still be there. Once there, we can part ways.\nTerenthis will want to hear your version of the story immediately, so head to Auberdine after we make it out of here.","rew":"You will receive:\nSteadfast Cinch\nMoney: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"‹name›! I'm pleased to see you've returned successfully. Your assistance to Volcor has given me faith that we can overcome the challenges facing us here in Darkshore and beyond.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":45,"y":85.3,"n":"Volcor","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":39.4,"y":43.5,"n":"Terenthis","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"92754":{"id":92754,"t":"A new need for shadow protection","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Greater Shadow Protection Potions to Mirda in the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3 Greater Shadow Protection Potion\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"Our clanmates continue to venture further south, to and beyond the cursed Valley of Bones.\nDespite your standing with our clan, I do not trust you enough to share the details of their ventures. They would be boring to you anyway, outsider.\nWhat matters to you is our need for Greater Shadow Protection Potions, in bulk, to ensure their continued survival. Bring some to me, and I will put in a good word for you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRecipe: Greater Spellblasting Potion Recipe: Greater Frenzy Potion\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+1,000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 92754","cats":["desolace"]},"94914":{"id":94914,"t":"Moonglade","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.","desc":"All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade. Keeper Remulos - Moonglade's guardian - keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.\nAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.","done":"Ah I see that you have already mastered the form of the Bear. Good, good. You are well on your way, young ‹class›.\nStormwind City Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":21,"y":55.4,"n":"Sheldras Moontree","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"834":{"id":834,"t":"Winds in the Desert","lv":9,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve 5 Sacks of Supplies and return them to Rezlak near Orgrimmar.\n5 Sack of Supplies Stolen Supply Sack","desc":"I'm Rezlak, one of Gazlowe's boys. Boss sent me to help the orcs here in Durotar. Things'd been going good except for the caravans. Can't manage to keep them safe! Makes my job a little harder, you know?\nThe last shipment--they promised it'd get through!--was snatched by the Dustwind harpies of...where was it...Razorwind Canyon?\nI gotta have those supplies or I'll never get anything done! Follow the big canyon to the south, you'll find the ravine cut right into the west and east sides of the walls.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"I'm great at what I do, don't get me wrong, but this is ridiculous! What am I supposed to do, build sand castles?","done":"Hey, now isn't that just the thing! You've got our supplies back for us. That's great. I'll be able to get back to work just as soon as I can find someone to haul these sacks for me.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":46.4,"y":22.9,"n":"Rezlak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"114":{"id":114,"t":"The Escape","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Invisibility Liquor to Maybell Maclure.\nInvisibility Liquor\nProvided: Invisibility Liquor","desc":"Take this invisibility liquor to young Maybell. It should last long enough for her to visit Tommy Joe.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Minor Healing Potion\nExperience: 800\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you deliver my letter to Tommy Joe? What did he say??","done":"Oh...my! I feel guilty deceiving my family, but my feelings for Tommy Joe are too strong to ignore.\nThank you, ‹name›. I'll drink this liquor as soon as I have the chance and sneak away to my love.\nAnd for you... please take this.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"William Pestle","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.2,"y":89.6,"n":"Maybell Maclure","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3634":{"id":3634,"t":"Gnome Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Gnome Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Engineering at the expert level breaks into two disciplines: gnome and goblin. While I think it is a waste, you should be aware of gnome specialization. They make items and gadgets that claim to change the world, but rarely often work.\n‹name›, read this manual. If you wish to learn how to make metal paper weights, then take that manual to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure you are sure before finishing his task!","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"Yes, yes, what needs of yours might I address today? Clearly, I have the time to do such since all I do is stand here while our beloved city lies in a cloud of irradiated death.","done":"Ah, a young engineer interested in pursuing the one, true discipline of engineering! Well forgive my melodrama, friend. While our situation remains dire, it still is always a good day to see another engineer respond to the clarion call of true engineering!\nThe Barrens Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tinkerwiz","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Tinkmaster Overspark","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4114":{"id":4114,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":50.6,"y":13.9,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8194":{"id":8194,"t":"Apprentice Angler","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0. Requires level 1 instead of 10.","obj":"5 Speckled Tastyfish","rew":"Money: 23 0 gold, 23 silver, 0 copper","back":"Even though we already have a contest winner, I will still buy your Tastyfish from you at a reasonable price. Whadda ya say!","done":"This deal works for me if it works for you!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.4,"y":76.8,"n":"Jang","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"7634":{"id":7634,"t":"Ancient Sinew Wrapped Lamina","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 10,900, 0.91 times as much.","obj":"Hastat the Ancient has asked that you bring him a Mature Blue Dragon Sinew. Should you find this sinew, return it to Hastat in Felwood.\nMature Blue Dragon Sinew Azuregos , Manaclaw 1 % , Cobalt Mageweaver 0.5 % , Cobalt Scalebane 0.5 % and 3 more","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. I am Hastat, Ancient of Lore. I hold knowledge lost eons ago.\nWith the proper binding, one of my leaves can serve as a quiver the likes of which has not been seen in 10,000 years. A quiver that when accompanied by a bow of Ancients, could grant untold powers.\nReturn here with sinew from an adult blue dragon and this quiver shall be yours.","rew":"You will receive:\nAncient Sinew Wrapped Lamina\nExperience: 9,950","back":"Welcome back, young ‹class›.","done":"May my leaves provide your arrows protection from harm. May your arrows strike true. May the enemies of our world be smitten.\nWinterspring Open the zone on the world map Start Hastat the Ancient End Hastat the Ancient Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Hunter Type Raid Shareable No Quest ID 7634\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 19,900 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Ancient Leaf\nFind the owner of the Ancient Petrified Leaf.\nAncient Petrified Leaf\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Ancient Sinew Wrapped Lamina this quest\nHastat the Ancient has asked that you bring him a Mature Blue Dragon Sinew.\nHastat the Ancient\n9,950 XP","cats":["hunter"]},"9154":{"id":9154,"t":"Light's Hope Chapel","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0.","obj":"Deliver the Call to Arms Announcement to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCall to Arms Announcement\nProvided: Call to Arms Announcement","desc":"The Scourge have returned in greater numbers than we have seen before. This must be the doing of the Lich King! The Argent Dawn is recruiting all willing and capable men and women to defend our lands.\nIf we share common cause, take this document to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.","back":"You've come to join our order, have you not?","done":"The Argent Dawn placed the call for aid, and you, among others, have answered. There is no time for us to provide you with training. Our faith is placed in your abilities, and that you will join us in throwing back this Scourge threat.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City Undercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.9,"y":31,"n":"Argent Recruiter","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":45.3,"n":"Argent Recruiter","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.2,"y":72.3,"n":"Argent Recruiter","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":66.2,"y":46.7,"n":"Argent Scout","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.5,"y":73.7,"n":"Argent Scout","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":43,"y":58.7,"n":"Argent Scout","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Keeper of the Rolls","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"274":{"id":274,"t":"A Dark Threat Looms","lv":18,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ashlan Stonesmirk wants you to return to Chief Engineer Hinderweir and inform him of the new discovery.\nDisarming Colloid\nProvided: Disarming Colloid","desc":"This ain't no ordinary blast powder. Look at the tiny silver crystals. And the distinct smell! Why it's clear as daylight that this is Seaforium Powder. Seaforium is harmless enough. But once it's wet it could blow Ironforge out of the mountain.\nThe chemical reaction can be defused by mixing four components: lurker venom, crushed Mo'Grosh crystal, a crocolisk tear and this disarming colloid. Now tell Hinderweir before it's too late!","rew":"Experience: 340\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","back":"What is that you bring from Ashlan?","done":"A disarming colloid? For Seaforium? Oh heavens!\nWetlands Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":50,"y":18.2,"n":"Ashlan Stonesmirk","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":46,"y":13.6,"n":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8674":{"id":8674,"t":"Winterhoof the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":26.5,"y":76.5,"n":"Elder Winterhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1954":{"id":1954,"t":"The Infernal Orb","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring an Infernal Orb to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\nInfernal Orb Burning Blade Summoner 55 %","desc":"The first step is to acquire an orb with power. The warlocks of the Burning Blade have nice, high quality orbs... it's too bad they've bound demons into them! But we can fix that, yes we can.\nGo to Desolace and snatch an infernal orb from a Burning Blade summoner. You'll find summoners at the Mannoroc Coven.\nWhen you have the orb, return to me.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","back":"Do you have an infernal orb, ‹name›?","done":"Oh, that's a nice one! No, I don't mean it's \"nice\" like cool juice is nice on a hot day.\nIn fact, it's very NOT nice now that I think about it. Not the juice. The orb!\nFocus, ‹name›! We'll need you focused if we're ever to finish our task!","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"754":{"id":754,"t":"Winterhoof Cleansing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Winterhoof Cleansing Totem at the Winterhoof Water Well, then return to Mull Thunderhorn.\nProvided: Winterhoof Cleansing Totem","desc":"I have crafted the totem to cleanse the Winterhoof Water Well. Now, you must take it to the well and perform a cleansing ritual. You will find it to the southeast, guarded by foul goblins!\nThis will not be an easy task, but you must do it if we are ever to use its waters again.\nFortune to you, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Do not delay, ‹name›. The Winterhoof Well's taint must be removed!","done":"News of your deed reached me moments ago -- already the beasts near the well drink from it eagerly.\nYou have done a great thing for the land, ‹name›. And you have done a great thing for the Tauren people.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.5,"y":63.6,"n":"Mull Thunderhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9074":{"id":9074,"t":"Earthshatter Girdle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rimblat Earthshatter at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make an Earthshatter Girdle if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Girdle, 8 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 3 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Girdle Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n3 Nexus Crystal","desc":"Would you honor me by returning the armor of those that fell in the defense of these lands?\nThe armor has been desecrated and is undoubtedly being used for evil; however, with wartorn armor scraps, the desecrated armor can be renewed and worn for battle once more.\nBring me the remnants of the fallen along with purification materials and Earthshatter shall be yours to don.\nSearch Naxxramas.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarthshatter Girdle\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Earthshatter Girdle.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":49.4,"n":"Rimblat Earthshatter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9234":{"id":9234,"t":"Icebane Gauntlets","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Frozen Runes, 12 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 2 Essences of Water and 200 gold.\n5 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n12 Thorium Bar\n2 Arcanite Bar\n2 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create Icebane gauntlets. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nIcebane Gauntlets","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8914":{"id":8914,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Beaststalker's Bindings to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\n15 Silithus Venom Sample Stonelash Scorpid 30 % , Stonelash Pincer 30 % , Stonelash Flayer 30 % , Sand Skitterer 30 % and 1 more\nBeaststalker's Bindings Fleshflayer Ghoul 4.3 % in Stratholme , Ghoul Ravener 4 % in Stratholme , Crimson Defender 2 % in Stratholme , Rage Talon Dragonspawn 1.7 %","desc":"Hail, ‹class›! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.\nPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.\nI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","rew":"You will receive:\nBeastmaster's Bindings\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you obtained the items I require, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. Mux will be quite happy with this.\nThose bindings were part of a larger armor set. If you're interested in providing me with further assistance, I'd be willing to consider parting with the rest of it.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"94434":{"id":94434,"t":"A lesson in divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.\n10 Linen Cloth","desc":"Wait, you want to... help? Why would a paladin want to help a beggar like me?\nWell, I suppose that you could be of some assistance.\nIts my wife you see. She, well... she's falling apart. I mean that literally. The apothecaries can stitch her back together right as rain, but they are about the Dark Lady's business and none are available to help. If you could perhaps bring me some fresh cloth then I could at least make her a wrapping to hold her together while we wait for the apothecaries.","back":"I hope that this is no imposition upon you, goodly ‹class›.","done":"This is very kind of you, ‹class›. Very kind indeed.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":65.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Tanis Alderwood","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"1794":{"id":1794,"t":"The Tome of Valor","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nTome of Valor","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.8,"y":22.1,"n":"Brandur Ironhammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5634":{"id":5634,"t":"Desperate Prayer","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.","desc":"A priest recently visited our halls seeking you out, young ‹race›. He said that he was on a mission to find you and that you should return to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. When you arrive, seek out High Priest Rohan--he will tell you more.\nThe Light be with you, ‹name›.","rew":"You will learn: Desperate Prayer","done":"You have done the Light a great service by becoming a shining example to those who travel in these dangerous lands and beyond. Please, accept this lesson as a thanks for all you've done.\nDarnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":40.3,"y":88.7,"n":"Lariia","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.8,"y":26.4,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"34":{"id":34,"t":"An Unwelcome Guest","lv":24,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Martie Jainrose of Lakeshire wants you to kill Bellygrub. Bring her his tusk as proof.\nBellygrub's Tusk Bellygrub","desc":"Once again my garden was trampled and pillaged. And I know the brute who is doing it. It's that forsaken boar, the one Marshal Marris has taken to calling Bellygrub.\nI won't be able to re-plant the daffodils until next season now. Ruined! All ruined by that one menacing boar. Put an end to that pest! Show me his tusk and I'd be happy to reward you. He seems to spend his time foraging in the field southwest of Lakeshire but occasionally he roams over here and into my garden.","rew":"You will receive:\nBouquet of Scarlet Begonias\nMoney: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Is Bellygrub still at it or were you able to rid Lakeshire of the pest once and for all?","done":"Finally the menace is laid to rest! Thank you, ‹name›, you have done me a great service. The garden shall be in full bloom this season!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":16.8,"y":46.3,"n":"Martie Jainrose","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8834":{"id":8834,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Ironforge.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":28.6,"n":"Officer Ironbeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"8354":{"id":8354,"t":"Chicken Clucking for a Mint","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Do a chicken emote at Innkeeper Norman, and in exchange you'll receive an Undercity Mint!","desc":"Ah, trick-or-treating for a sick child, are we? I was going to say, you're a little old to be rummaging about for candies...\nWell, for my treat - an Undercity Mint - you will need to... cluck like a chicken! Yes, chickens love mints... well OK, maybe they don't LOVE them... but I won't give you a mint unless you chicken cluck for me!\nWell ‹class›, are you up to the challenge or not?! Time to earn your treat!","rew":"You will receive:\nUndercity Mint","done":"Too funny! Well done, ‹name›! Here's your treat.\nHappy Hallow's End!\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":67.7,"y":37.9,"n":"Innkeeper Norman","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"81954":{"id":81954,"t":"Venomous journeys","lv":45,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Venomous Journeys","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 390","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nVenomous Journeys (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1074":{"id":1074,"t":"Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Nitromirglyceronium back to Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon.\nNG-5\nProvided: NG-5","desc":"Here you go, stranger. Take heed with it though... it's volatile stuff.\nIf you're really a friend of Gaxim's, then tell him I say hello. If you're not, then have fun blowin' yerself up.","rew":"Experience: 825\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Ah, goodie goodie, you're back.","done":"Your task has been done flawlessly, ‹name›.\nNG-5 is the unequivocal component in the recipe to ignite the wagons of dynamite.\nWhat? Yes, dynamite... wagons of it. It's the perfect distraction, I tell you... just wait and see.\nDun Morogh Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.7,"y":29.4,"n":"Lomac Gearstrip","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"97234":{"id":97234,"t":"Reading room","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the wrapped reading material to the Stormwind library.\nProvided: Wrapped Reading Material","desc":"Are you here to discuss the deeper meanings of our storied legends? No?\nWell, after you're done looking around, can you carry this to the library for me? We're exchanging some of our less popular bodies of work for some more modern writing. I have a list of tomes I'm quite sure the librarian will be able to procure for us within our existing arrangement.\nComplimentary club refreshments on us, if you help us out.","back":"Please keep your voice down.","done":"Let's see here. Roy's Book Club, isn't it? I recognize this wrap technique.\nWell, if he says this is what people want to talk about, it's all fine by me. The material we receive back is always in as good of quality as we loaned it, so we know they're treating it with respect regardless of how provoking the words may be.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":62,"n":"Roy Lewells","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":71.6,"y":7.4,"n":"Donyal Tovald","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"434":{"id":434,"t":"The Attack!","lv":31,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Remain in the garden until Lord Gregor Lescovar and Marzon the Silent Blade have had their conversation. Afterwards, kill them both before returning to Elling Trias in Stormwind.\nLord Gregor Lescovar slain\nMarzon the Silent Blade slain","desc":"After I put on Spybot's disguise, he'll head in to talk to Lescovar. The guards should let him pass no problem.\nWhile you were getting materials for me, I took care of informing Marzon that it was time for him and Lescovar to meet again. I even dropped some false information.\nLescovar will dismiss his guards and wait for Marzon out here in the garden. After you catch wind of talk about the Defias, make your move. You need to kill them both before the guards return! When you're done, speak to Trias.","rew":"Experience: 1,900\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes, ‹name›? Are things going well with Tyrion? He apprised me of the situation and I've helped him trick Marzon into going to the castle.\nMarzon has been a thorn in the side of many people in Stormwind; many of which are close friends of mine. No one messes with my friends... not if they know what's healthy for them.\nIt's just a shame I'm indirectly doing a favor for Shaw and SI:7 in the meantime. Oh well, not every plan is perfect.","done":"So it is done? Good. Thank you greatly for your discretion, ‹name›. You've proven worthy on more than one count. I'll be sure to keep my eyes on you and your progress within the Alliance.\nBe sure to keep your nose clean.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":73.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tyrion","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"7794":{"id":7794,"t":"A Donation of Mageweave","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. Such generosity would not go unnoticed by Stormwind, I assure you!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53.9,"y":81.7,"n":"Clavicus Knavingham","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"194":{"id":194,"t":"Raptor Mastery","lv":34,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hemet Nesingwary wants you to kill 10 Stranglethorn Raptors.\nStranglethorn Raptor slain : 0/ 10","desc":"So you think your hunting skills are in tip-top shape? I can put them to the test in a jiffy. Head out into that jungle and kill 10 Stranglethorn Raptors. We'll see just how much of a big game hunter you are.\nAnd no, I won't tell you where you can find them! Locating the beasts is half the challenge.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","back":"I never met a hunter who got any kills by standing around the campfire. Were you planning on killing those Stranglethorn Raptors or were you hoping they would die of old age?","done":"Nicely done, old chap!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"594":{"id":594,"t":"Message in a Bottle","lv":45,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the author of the message in a bottle.","desc":"The note reads, in fairly good handwriting:\nTo any that can aid me-\nPlease, my need for help is dire. A great Skymane holds me captive on an island in the South Seas.\nThe stars at night are foreign to me and obscured by the jungle trees, but on the clearest days I see Wild Shore to the northwest, and what seem to be large sailing ships to the southwest.\nI beg of you, my would-be savior, please help me.","rew":"Experience: 2,900","done":"Have you come to free me?","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.8,"y":78.7,"n":"Carefully Folded Note","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38.5,"y":80.6,"n":"Princess Poobah","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8754":{"id":8754,"t":"The Path of the Conqueror","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You honor my kind, ‹name›. Strike down the enemies of Kalimdor! Show them what it means to deface the land of eternal starlight.\nYou have earned another enhancement. Hand me your signet ring so that I may bolster its power.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the conqueror!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2994":{"id":2994,"t":"Saving Sharpbeak","lv":51,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 51 instead of 53. Gives 7,350 experience instead of 7,900, 0.93 times as much.","obj":"Fight to the top of Jintha'Alor, kill Vile Priestess Hexx for the key to Sharpbeak's cage, and save Sharpbeak.\nOpen Sharpbeak's Cage","desc":"We must save Sharpbeak!\nFight your way to the top of Jintha'Alor in the heart of Vilebranch territory, gain the key to Sharpbeak's cage from the vile Priestess Hexx, and then find and save Sharpbeak!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGryphon Rider's Stormhammer Gryphon Rider's Leggings\nMoney: 2 25 2 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,350\n+200 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"Save Sharpbeak!","done":"Swiftwind and Keenclaw returned with their child moments ago, and are fussing over him like new parents. Seeing them together again is enough to give even this old dwarf mist in the eyes...\nWe cannot repay you enough for what you have done, ‹name›. The gryphons of Aerie peak, and their riders, will sing your name for a long, long time.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":9.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Gryphon Master Talonaxe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1154":{"id":1154,"t":"Test of Lore","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Legacy of the Aspects and return it to Braug Dimspirit near the entrance to Talondeep Path in Stonetalon Mountains.\nLegacy of the Aspects The Legacy of the Aspects","desc":"You have passed Dorn's tests, and now you seek to pass your next trial. Very good. But up until now, your challenges have been childish. It is easy to test your body--your mind is another matter completely.\nI shall explain it simply: find the book I name, study it, and answer my question about its contents.\nWhat book, you must be asking? The Legacy of the Aspects. It can be found at the bottom of Dor'danil in southern Ashenvale, protected by the dead druids and their slayers.","rew":"Experience: 1,850\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Bring me the book after you've studied it. I will not ask you your question until after you have given me the book.","done":"This is the book I named. There is hope you will answer my question correctly then... unless you've forgotten to study its contents.\nWhen you are prepared, speak to me again and I shall ask a question of you.\nStonetalon Mountains Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":78.8,"y":45.7,"n":"Braug Dimspirit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1394":{"id":1394,"t":"Final Passage","lv":36,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.","desc":"You have done well, ‹name›. You have passed my test, and the tests before mine. Return to Dorn in Thousand Needles. He will sense the change within you, and see that your mind, body and spirit are strong enough that you should be rewarded for your efforts.\nStay true to the balance you've shown throughout these trials, ‹name›. Dorn will test you again in the future if you do.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWindstorm Hammer Dancing Flame\nExperience: 4,200\n+200 reputation with Horde","done":"Ah, ‹name›. It has been a long time since you have last stepped into my home. It seems like many moons have passed since you took your first leap that set you upon your path.\nAnd now you return to me stronger than you once were... more enlightened. This pleases me. And you should be justly rewarded for seeing my tests to the end.\nUndercity Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":57.8,"y":65.4,"n":"Parqual Fintallas","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":53.9,"y":41.5,"n":"Dorn Plainstalker","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"95314":{"id":95314,"t":"That shadowvale green elixir","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 8 Bottles of Whispering Elixir from Shadowvale, then return to Carolai Anise in Brill.\n8 Bottle of Whispering Elixir","desc":"Before the Scourge invasion, the reclusive village of Shadowvale was known for its Whispering Elixir. Distilled from herbs found only in Tyr's Fall, the elixir was sought by apothecaries, mystics, and poisoners alike even after being banned in the city.\nI've had requests from a number of buyers eager to get their hands on some elixir. Travel to the ruins of Shadowvale deep in the Whispering Forest to the west. I'm prepared to offer significant compensation if you can recover some bottles for me.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I trust you did not get lost?","done":"You say there is evil in Shadowvale? I admit, I am not surprised. The forest folk were an odd lot, and they did not care for visitors. Some believe the Whispering Forest itself is cursed, and the elixir distilled from its roots carries that same curse...\n...but enough of superstition and rumors, He. Thank you for the elixirs. Here, take this as payment.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.2,"n":"Carolai Anise","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"354":{"id":354,"t":"Deaths in the Family","lv":11,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Gregor's Remains, Nissa's Remains and Thurman's Remains to Coleman Farthing in Brill.\nGregor's Remains Gregor Agamand\nNissa's Remains Nissa Agamand\nThurman's Remains Thurman Agamand","desc":"The Agamand family was the most prosperous family in Tirisfal Glades. I used to work their mills...before the Plague.\nWhen the Scourge first came, the Agamands fortified their home and convinced those in their employ to remain and help them defend. We were fools, but at least we were loyal fools.\nThe Agamands, in their pride, doomed us to undeath. And now they are minions of the Scourge!\nServe the Forsaken by defeating the Agamands who fell to the Plague. Serve me by bringing me their remains.","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have the remains of the Agamands? Are those cursed beasts finally destroyed?","done":"Revenge has a sweet taste, don't you think? When you destroyed the Agamands, did you catch any hint of free will within them? I hope so. I hope they knew fear before they were smashed into oblivion.\nIt is a foolish hope, I know. But it is a hope I foster nonetheless.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":52.3,"n":"Coleman Farthing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"914":{"id":914,"t":"Leaders of the Fang","lv":22,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 10 instead of 11. Gives 4,300 experience instead of 2,200, 1.95 times as much. New rewards: Hammerbone. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring the Gems of Cobrahn, Anacondra, Pythas and Serpentis to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff.\nGem of Cobrahn Lord Cobrahn\nGem of Anacondra Lady Anacondra\nGem of Pythas Lord Pythas\nGem of Serpentis Lord Serpentis","desc":"The druids in the Wailing Caverns, the Druids of the Fang, are an aberration. They were part of an order of noble druids whose plan was to heal the Barrens, but now seek to remake that land to match their own, twisted dreams.\nThe Druids of the Fang have four leaders, and each possesses a dream gem. Even now their faces haunt me! Defeat the leaders and bring me their gems, and the Barrens may again know peace.\nGo, ‹name›. You will find them lurking deep within the Wailing Caverns.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCrescent Staff Wingblade Hammerbone\nNew in Forever: Hammerbone.\nExperience: 4,300\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Memories of my nightmares haunt me, ‹name›. Have you defeated the leaders of the fang and acquired their gems?","done":"You have done it, ‹name›. You killed the leaders of the Druids of the Fang. My dreams are now free of their wicked faces, and you have helped save the Barrens from a cursed future.\nI thank you, ‹name›. I thank you for myself, for the druids of Thunder Bluff, and for the land.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":75.6,"y":31.6,"n":"Nara Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"1474":{"id":1474,"t":"The Binding","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Pure Hearts, summon and subdue a succubus, then return the Pure Hearts to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.\nSummoned Succubus slain\nProvided: Pure Hearts","desc":"Using these hearts, cast a spell at the summoning circle to open a doorway for the succubus to come through. Your powers are greater now, and you will need all of them to defeat the succubus.\nBeware its charms, ‹name›, many a strong mind has been bound to its will. When overcome, the succubus will be returned to the void, and I will teach you the spell to summon it forth at your command.","rew":"You will receive:\nSmall Soul Pouch\nYou will learn: Summon Succubus\nExperience: 1,550","back":"Of the powers from beyond the void, the succubus is one of the most dangerous, as the weak are most easily wrapped around its fingers.\nRemember that now and in the future.","done":"Again, you have done well, ‹name›. It has been quite some time since I have seen a young warlock with as much potential as you. Be assured that I will continue to watch your progress, and prepare and assist you in your future trials.\nFor now, let me show you the summoning spell for your newly dominated succubus.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":26,"n":"Carendin Halgar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1714":{"id":1714,"t":"Essence of the Exile","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"8 Thundering Charm Thundering Exile 50 % , Drywhisker Kobold 0.4 % , Drywhisker Digger 0.3 % , Drywhisker Surveyor 0.3 %\n8 Burning Charm Burning Exile 47 % , Drywhisker Digger 0.3 % , Drywhisker Kobold 0.3 % , Drywhisker Surveyor 0.3 %\n8 Cresting Charm Cresting Exile 50.1 % , Drywhisker Surveyor 0.3 % , Drywhisker Kobold 0.3 % , Drywhisker Digger 0.3 %","rew":"You will receive:\nEssence of the Exile","back":"The cauldron bubbles. Its vapors beckon...","done":"The charms sink slowly into the cauldron's depths...\nA large bubble rises to the surface of the liquid and breaks...\n...And a churning lump of molten rock is revealed.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":79.3,"y":66.8,"n":"Bath'rah's Cauldron","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"7874":{"id":7874,"t":"Quell the Silverwing Usurpers","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,750 experience instead of 3,300, 0.83 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Alliance, gain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and bring it to Captain Shatterskull at the Mor'shan Base Camp.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The wilds of the Ashenvale forest will succumb to the might of the Horde, ‹race›. Nothing the Silverwing say or do can stop our sovereign imperative. Kalimdor belongs to the Horde. How dare they attempt to prevent us from harvesting what is rightfully ours!\nLet the pride swell in your chest as you cut down their weak attempts at slowing our progress. Destroy the Silverwing Sentinels, and earn a Warsong mark of honor. Return to me with such a mark, ‹name›, and you will be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 1 10 1 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The blood of our enemies is a mark of honor. Do you have such a mark?","done":"<Captain Shatterskull roars in triumph.>\nHow much more can they withstand? How many more Alliance filth must perish at the hands of the Horde for them to retreat? Only time will tell, ‹race›.\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Orc, Undead, Tauren, Troll Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7874","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"8434":{"id":8434,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Experience: 3,200\n+50 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5234":{"id":5234,"t":"Return to the Bulwark","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Writhing Haunt Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at The Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nFilled Writhing Haunt Bottle\nProvided: Filled Writhing Haunt Bottle","desc":"You delicately top off the empty bottle; a sample of the foul substance that churns under the platform of the cauldron now oozes back and forth inside the fragile glass container.\nWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark to complete the mission.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+50 reputation with Undercity\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Once we successfully analysis the sample drawn from the Writhing Haunt's cauldron, it will provide us with a third avenue to deliver a devastating counter agent against the Scourge!","done":"Another finely executed mission, ‹name›! This makes three cauldrons available to us to turn against the Scourge. If Kel'Thuzad's necromantic dominance over these lands wasn't as strong as it currently is, I'd dare say you'd shut them down completely!\nApothecary Dithers will have a report on what this cauldron - as well as the other cauldrons subverted - will require to deliver our counter agent to the plague. With that, the time has come to bring the last cauldron of the west under our influence!\nWestern Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53,"y":65.6,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5154":{"id":5154,"t":"The Annals of Darrowshire","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Annals of Darrowshire to Chromie in Andorhal.\nAnnals of Darrowshire Musty Tome","desc":"To save Joseph Redpath, we must first discover his past. We can learn this in the Annals of Darrowshire, a book held in the city hall of Andorhal.\nBring me that book. We can then learn Joseph's fate, and with luck... change it!","rew":"Experience: 5,800","back":"Did you find the book, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, you found it!\nDid you read it? Is Joseph Redpath mentioned? If he is, then perhaps we can save him!\nAh. The Annals of Darrowshire tell a very unsettling tale. It says that during the battle, Joseph Redpath was corrupted and joined the ranks of the Scourge! He then betrayed the defenders of Darrowshire.\nThat is an ill fate. If we can, we should try to change that fate, don't you think?","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.5,"y":66.8,"n":"Chromie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92514":{"id":92514,"t":"Welcome to shendar village","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Illaya Amberwind and Coriella Calmbreeze in Shen'dar Village.\nSpeak with Illaya Amberwind\nSpeak with the Innkeeper","desc":"You've got that \"Windshaper\" air about you. Something about how I can feel a tiny bit of static on my skin when near someone spirit-touched that gives it away. Before I properly put you to work around here, you should check in with our resident Windshaper elder, Illaya Amberwind. She's just outside, near the center of town.\nOh, and check in with Coriella Calmbreeze as well, she runs the local inn and can provide lodging and supplies, should you need them.","done":"Checked in with Illaya then? Great. Lots of tension between the High Order and the Windshapers these days, but they keep things civil here in Shen'dar. Everyone here is well aware that we've got bigger problems than their quibbles.\nNow that that's done, you look like someone who might be looking for something to do with their hands and I've got a bandit problem that I was hoping you could help me with.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92834":{"id":92834,"t":"Avenged tenfold","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Al'Aketh Windstone Charms from Al'Aketh cultists found north of Valanaar at the Gustberry Fields or Shrine of Akir.\n10 Al'Aketh Windstone Charm","desc":"When the cult began their campaign of violence, the Peacekeepers and Windshapers responded with posturing. I saw this as foolish escalation so I advocated for peaceful dialogue. Yesterday I dispatched my friend Belathaan Brightwish to the Shrine of Akir, hoping to establish that dialogue.\nA box just arrived containing Belathaan's tongue, dipped in silver pigment.\nIts clear to me now that there is no reasoning with the cult. Kill any cultists you see, and bring me the prayer charms that they carry.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMartyr's Armor Sash of Sorrow Cilice of Regret\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"The mark of a leader is the ability to admit when they were wrong. I don't agree with the Windshapers often, but they were right to dismiss the idea of trying to engage peacefully with the Al'Aketh. My attempt to take the high road cost a dear friend his life and is a mistake I will have to live with for the rest of my days.","done":"The High Order prides ourselves in our pragmatism and logic, and logic dictates that the avoidance of conflict and loss of life is the most prudent option in most situations.\n<Elaadrin's eyes begin to glow and crackle with arcane energy.>\n...however, the cult mistook our prudence for weakness and they are not nearly ready to pay the cost of that error.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});